Add a FLOW_ACTION_SAMPLE dispatch to the DSA matchall classifier offload,
following the existing mirred and police entries. A new pair of switch
ops, port_sample_add/port_sample_del, receives a pre-parsed sample entry
(direction, 1-in-N rate, truncation parameters and the psample group the
samples are to be delivered to).

Both the ingress and the egress qdisc are accepted; whether a driver
supports either direction is its own decision. Since the hardware of
typical switch ASICs provides a single sampler per port and direction,
replacing a filter replaces the programmed sampler in place instead of
rejecting the new rule.

The psample group pointer is borrowed from the action; drivers that cache
it for their data path must take their own reference with
psample_group_take().


